// ALIAS-COLLAPSE (Foundation C): a `sort`/`const`/`func`/`pred` alias binds the local
// name to the TARGET's EXISTING pool Index (identity by origin, mints nothing). So the
// aliased `op`/`E` are the SAME entities as `src.op`/`src.E`, and a proof stated in the
// local vocabulary matches the source axiom cited across the alias boundary — no sort
// mismatch (the local `G` and `src.G` collapse to one Index).
import src <<< "alias_ident_source.bpa"

sort G = src.G
const E = src.E
func op = src.op
pred good = src.good

theorem leftId: forall a: G; op(E, a) = a
proof
  @goal | forall a: G; op(E, a) = a [by axiom src.opIdentityLeft]
qed
